# Redirects are intentionally NOT handled here:
#
#  - `/` → `/en-au/`  is generated by Astro (astro.config.mjs `redirects`),
#    emitted as dist/index.html. Defining it here too triggers Cloudflare's
#    "Duplicate rule for path /" error.
#  - www → apex (lumii.com.au)  is an EDGE redirect (Cloudflare Redirect Rule),
#    not a file rule: Workers static-assets `_redirects` rejects absolute URLs
#    ("Only relative URLs are allowed"), and host-to-host belongs at the edge
#    anyway. See README "Needs Garth → Cloudflare → custom domains".
#
# Add only RELATIVE, in-site path redirects below (e.g. /old-path /new-path 301).
